Statements:
[
    "To understand how MMLU Pro improved on the original MMLU, let's first break down what MMLU Pro aimed to achieve.",
    "The original MMLU, or Massive Multitask Language Understanding benchmark, was a foundational assessment tool in the field of Large Language Models (LLMs).",
    "It had its limitations and challenges, which became apparent as it started to saturate.",
    "Saturation means that the benchmark was no longer able to effectively distinguish between the capabilities of different models, as many models began to achieve high scores.",
    "MMLU Pro was designed to address some of the shortcomings of the original MMLU.",
    "One of the primary improvements was in the structure of the questions.",
    "In the original MMLU, each multiple-choice question (MCQ) had 4 options.",
    "In contrast, MMLU Pro increased the number of options to 10 for each question.",
    "This change significantly increased the difficulty level.",
    "Models now had to be more precise in selecting the correct answer from a larger pool of options.",
    "This adjustment was intended to provide a more nuanced assessment of a model's understanding and ability to reason.",
    "It required the model to not just recognize the correct answer but also to effectively rule out more incorrect options.",
    "Another significant change was the reduction in the number of subjects covered.",
    "The original MMLU encompassed 57 subjects, which was later reduced to 12 subjects in MMLU Pro.",
    "This reduction allowed for a deeper focus on these core subjects.",
    "It enabled a more in-depth evaluation of a model's knowledge and understanding within these areas.",
    "By concentrating on a smaller set of subjects, MMLU Pro aimed to assess not just the breadth of knowledge but also the depth of understanding that a model possessed.",
    "The tagline for MMLU Pro, 'MMLU Rebuilt to fix its flaws,' encapsulates the essence of these improvements.",
    "By addressing the limitations of the original MMLU, such as the ease with which models could achieve high scores due to the smaller number of options and the broad range of subjects, MMLU Pro offered a more challenging and comprehensive assessment tool.",
    "This evolution reflects the ongoing effort in the field of LLM evaluations to create benchmarks that can effectively measure the capabilities and limitations of language models, pushing the boundaries of what these models can achieve."
] 

